ZERO screen-reader / internal engine

CORE
  The screen reader is not an external dependency.
  It consumes semantic events generated by the ZERO browser.

EVENT
  event := target + role + name + state + relation + location + cause

PIPELINES
  semantic -> speech
  semantic -> braille
  semantic -> keyboard state

SPEECH
  queueable
  interruptible
  resumable
  prioritized
  context-aware

NAVIGATION
  document
  headings
  landmarks
  links
  controls
  tables
  lists
  paragraphs
  alerts
  history

RULE
  Never infer accessibility from pixels when semantic information exists.
  Never make speech the canonical representation.

FAILURE
  Missing semantics are reported as missing semantics.
  The engine does not invent labels merely to hide uncertainty.

TEST
  Every browser action must produce inspectable semantic events.
  Every semantic event must be representable in speech and braille.
